"the same key are omitted and a single log entry is generated. This allows "
"administrators to more easily keep track of attackers that try to brute "
"force API authentication, by reducing the noise generated by expired API "
"keys. On the other hand, this makes little sense for internal MISP instances "
"where detecting the misconfiguration of tools becomes more interesting, so "
"if you fall into the latter category, enable this feature."
msgstr ""

